sub:Head {
    sub: a np:Nanopublication ;
        np:hasAssertion sub:assertion ;
        np:hasProvenance sub:provenance ;
        np:hasPublicationInfo sub:pubinfo .
}

sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-deflecta-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Drosophila deflecta detail-scale Turing wavelength (2.633 µm, pass 1) faithfully reproduces Drosophila deflecta morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-deflecta-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila deflecta specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-deflecta-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-deflecta-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/drosophila_deflecta_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Drosophila deflecta; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing (1952) derived the diffusion-driven instability and the critical wavenumber. Schnakenberg (1979) gave the two-species kinetics. | Werner et al. (2010) showed Wingless at vein intersections paints spots in D. guttifera. Prud'homme et al. (2006) showed the D. elegans apical spot is a yellow cis-regulatory novelty.; reconstructed_in_script: Nondimensional parameters (a, b, D_u, D_v) = (0.132, 0.780, 0.061, 3.050) are chosen for this 2.633 µm slot. They are not measurements from those papers. | Detail-tier wavelengths of D. cyrtoloma and D. elegans are the primordium-tier catalog lengths rescaled by 207.6/108.8 and 101.1/108.8 onto 2.633 µm.; transfer_boundary: Wingless vein spots were shown in D. guttifera, not as a 2.633 µm wavelength in D. deflecta. The chronoseries radiation label is the assigned bucket; D. deflecta is a quinaria-group fly.; does_not_claim: Does not claim a wet-lab measurement of a 2.633 µm pigment wavelength on D. deflecta. | Does not claim the pass-1 unforced GIF is a pixel fit to the gallery spiral.]; phenomenon_size: 1.9 µm (1.919e-06 m, log10=-5.717 m, tier=3_subcellular_um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 1.9 µm to 4.3 mm): 1.9 µm:drosophila-affinis-bioelectric-polarity, 6.0 µm:drosophila-affinis-vertex-packing, 96 µm:drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength, 192 µm:drosophila-affinis-clock-wavefront, 432 µm:drosophila-affinis-morphogen-condensation, 528 µm:drosophila-affinis-elastic-buckling, 600 µm:drosophila-affinis-flux-canalization, 840 µm:drosophila-affinis-branching-tree" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature04597>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature08896>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1179047> .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-deflecta-turing-wavelength-s0.py> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-deflecta-turing-wavelength-s0.py" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> ;
        schema:programmingLanguage "Python" .
}

